course: dictionary
lesson: 2584
title: Words for cloth and clothes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Denim is the name of a strong cloth, usually blue. Many jeans, jackets and skirts are made from it. «Denim for jeans is woven with blue-dyed threads one way and white threads the other.» Woven means the threads are crossed over and under each other to make the cloth.
explain: Denim can also name the clothes themselves. Its plural, denims, is an informal word for jeans. If someone says «I'm wearing my denims today», they mean their jeans. Ask yourself: does the sentence mean the cloth or the clothes?
explain: Phrases give you clues too. A «denim jacket» is a jacket made of denim, and «blue denim» tells you the colour. If the sentence talks about wearing, washing or cutting, denim probably means the cloth or the clothes made from it.
fact: Denim is a strong cotton cloth, usually blue.
fact: Denim is woven in a twill pattern, which makes diagonal lines across the cloth.
fact: Denim is dyed with indigo, which is why jeans fade over time.
fact: In 1873, Levi Strauss and Jacob Davis made strong denim trousers for miners and workers in the American West.
fact: «Denims» is an informal plural word that means jeans.
exercise: «Denim for jeans is woven with blue-dyed threads one way and white threads the other.» What is denim? | A type of paper | A soft wool used for knitting | *A strong cotton cloth, usually blue | A kind of shoe
exercise: Ella says, «I'm wearing my denims today.» What are denims here? | *Jeans | A metal tool | A sheet of paper | A pair of gloves
exercise: In «denim shorts», what is the word denim describing? | Very long shorts for swimming | Shorts that are shiny and metal | Shorts made of thin silk | *Shorts made of strong blue cotton cloth
test:
Why do jeans fade over time? | *Because they are dyed with indigo, which wears away with washing and wear | Because they are made of paper that gets wet | Because the cloth shrinks in the sun | Because they are painted with red dye that runs
test:
Who made strong denim trousers for miners and workers in 1873? | Queen Victoria | *Levi Strauss and Jacob Davis | Thomas Edison | Nadia and Leo
exam:
In «blue denim», what does the word blue tell us? | *The colour of the cloth | The price of the jeans | The size of the jeans | The name of a shop
